+## Isolated migration acceptance: lease lifetime
+
+A concurrent fork can temporarily retain a connection lock descriptor before
+exec, even with O_CLOEXEC. Lease destruction now explicitly unlocks the flock,
+so a completed rotation can immediately reacquire its lock. The lock inode stays
+persistent. A deterministic duplicate-descriptor regression covers both shared
+and exclusive leases and confirms that the replacement lease still fences
+other readers/writers. Linux flock semantics: https://man7.org/linux/man-pages/man2/flock.2.html.
